<header><h1>📁 File System Guide</h1><p>Organize your digital study materials.</p></header>
<main>
<section><h2>What is a File?</h2><p>A file stores information such as text, pictures, videos or program code.</p></section>
<section><h2>What is a Folder?</h2><p>A folder groups files and other folders to keep information organized.</p></section>
<section>
<h2>Common File Extensions</h2>
<ul>
<li><code>.html</code> — Web page</li>
<li><code>.css</code> — Web page styling</li>
<li><code>.py</code> — Python source code</li>
<li><code>.txt</code> — Plain text</li>
<li><code>.pdf</code> — Portable document</li>
<li><code>.jpg</code> — Image file</li>
<li><code>.mp3</code> — Audio file</li>
<li><code>.xlsx</code> — Excel workbook</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section><h2>Example Folder Structure</h2>
<p>📁 College Work</p>
<p>　📁 HTML Projects</p>
<p>　　📄 index.html</p>
<p>　　📄 style.css</p>
<p>　📁 Notes</p>
<p>　　📄 computer_notes.pdf</p>
</section>
<section><h2>Organization Tip 💡</h2><p>Use meaningful filenames, create subject-wise folders and keep a backup of important work.</p></section>
</main>
</body>
